## Key Learnings from Day 7

- Claude has **three distinct models** (Haiku, Sonnet, Opus) serving different complexity and speed needs — choosing the right one is as important as the prompt itself.
- **Effort level** is a separate dimension from model choice and dramatically affects output depth for complex tasks.
- The **"right tool for the task"** mindset applies to AI just like it does to any professional tool.
- **Prompt quality** matters more than model choice for most everyday tasks — a great prompt on Sonnet beats a vague prompt on Opus.
- Heavy users should think in **workflows**, not single prompts: research → synthesize → draft → refine → finalize.
- Saving a personal Claude strategy (like this one) and referring to it regularly prevents the #1 mistake: using the same model/effort for everything.

